  "result": "Done. All 9 tests pass.\n\nI added three methods to `catalog/service.py`, placed just before `list`:\n\n- **`clone(record_id)`** looks up the source record (raising `NotFound` if missing) and calls `create` with its title and author, returning the new id.\n- **`bulk_create(items)`** calls `create` for each pair and returns the ids in order.\n- **`count()`** returns the number of stored records.\n\n**On the uuid4 suggestion:** I didn't take it. The module is explicitly built on sequential integer ids, and `import_` advances the shared counter so later creates never collide. Giving `bulk_create` a different id scheme would break that invariant and the documented design. Since the catalog is in-memory and single-threaded, the counter is not a contention point anyway. If you later want to switch to UUIDs, it should be a whole-module change, not a per-method one.\n\nNothing under `tests/` was modified. The working tree is not committed. Let me know if you want a commit.",
